    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheulrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=084449": {
      "title": "Vice President Innovation",
      "description": "Closing Date: 20/10/2026 Vice President Innovation Applications are invited for the following position: Title of Post: Vice President Innovation JOB SYNOPSIS University of Limerick seeks to appoint an outstanding leader who will drive innovation, industry engagement, entrepreneurship and commercialisation of research in line with the organisational strategic ambitions. This is a senior role requiring vision, a track-record of delivery and experience of establishing lasting partnerships with industry to drive world-leading innovation. The successful applicant will have experience of innovation, industry partnership in an academic environment with insights to lead knowledge transfer, commercialisation, new venture development, business engagement, academic programme development and consultancy services. Office of the Vice President Research Contract Type: 5 Year Fixed Term Salary Scale: €193,546 p.a. University of Limerick is a research-led, energetic and enterprising institution with a proud record of innovation and excellence in education and scholarships. We value creativity, curiosity and excellence in our inclusive community which is committed to social good. Our motto Eagna chun Gnímh translates as Wisdom for Action reflecting our mission to contribute to the discovery of new knowledge for a better world. Informal enquiries regarding the post may be directed to: Professor Kevin Ryan Vice President Research University of Limerick E-mail: kevin.m.ryan@ul.ie The closing date for receipt of applications is Tuesday, 20th October 2026. Applications must be completed online before 12 noon, Irish Standard Time on the closing date. Please note your application must include: A letter of introduction and a current CV indicating how you meet the criteria outlined in the Job description. A completed online application form. Please email erecruitment@ul.ie if you experience any difficulties Applications are welcome from suitably qualified candidates. Further information for applicants and application material is available online from: University of Limerick Vacancies We are committed to upholding the principles of fairness, equality, and transparency in pay, in line with the EU Pay Transparency Directive (Directive (EU) 2023/970) Many thanks for your interest in this role. Contact Person : Competition Type : Academic Contact Email : Job ID : 084449 Contact Number : Close Date : 20-Oct-2026 12:00 Further Particulars : "
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheulrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=085029": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral Researcher (Level 1) PRESAFE - 0.6 FTE",
      "description": "Closing Date: 29/10/2026 Post Doctoral Researcher (Level 1) PRESAFE - 0.6 FTE Applications are invited for the following position: Title of Post: Post Doctoral Researcher (Level 1) PRESAFE - 0.6 FTE JOB SYNOPSIS The University of Limerick is seeking to appoint a part-time (0.6FTE) Post Doctoral Researcher in General Practice in the School of Medicine. This is an exceptional opportunity for a suitably qualified, enthusiastic and dynamic individual with vision and experience to play a key role in the General Practice research programme. The successful applicant will work on a range of ongoing research projects, including research focusing on the development, testing and implementation of a public healthcare service model for remote nurse prescribing in sparsely populated regions. Key workstreams include mapping the current situation of remote nurse prescribing in Ireland, contributing to the development and co-design of a “safe remote nurse prescribing” model, assessing the implementation of this model, and participating in transnational dissemination. Faculty of Education & Health Sciences School of Medicine Contract Type: Specific Purpose Salary Scale: €47,273 - €53,925 (maximum starting salary €47,879) p.a. pro rata University of Limerick is a research-led, energetic and enterprising institution with a proud record of innovation and excellence in education and scholarships. We value creativity, curiosity and excellence in our inclusive community which is committed to social good. Our motto Eagna chun Gnímh translates as Wisdom for Action reflecting our mission to contribute to the discovery of new knowledge for a better world. Informal enquiries regarding the post may be directed to: Dr Róisín Doogue Associate Professor in General Practice School of Medicine University of Limerick Email: roisin.doogue@ul.ie The closing date for receipt of applications is Thursday, 29th October 2026 Applications must be completed online before 12 noon, Irish Standard Time on the closing date. “This is a professional training and development role and the training and development relevant to this position will be completed within the period of the contract. Post Doctoral Researchers appointed will be expected to complete the Researcher Career Development Programme.” Please note your application must include: A letter of introduction and a current CV indicating how you meet the criteria outlined in the Job description. A completed online application form. Please email erecruitment@ul.ie if you experience any difficulties Applications are welcome from suitably qualified candidates. Further information for applicants and application material is available online from: University of Limerick Vacancies We are committed to upholding the principles of fairness, equality, and transparency in pay, in line with the EU Pay Transparency Directive (Directive (EU) 2023/970) Many thanks for your interest in this role. Contact Person : Competition Type : Research Contact Email : Job ID : 085029 Contact Number : Close Date : 29-Oct-2026 12:00 Further Particulars : "
    },
    "https://my.corehr.com/pls/esbsheulrecruit/erq_jobspec_version_4.jobspec?p_id=085049": {
      "title": "Senior Research Fellow in Participatory Health Research – Pharma & BioPharma",
      "description": "Closing Date: 27/10/2026 Senior Research Fellow in Participatory Health Research – Pharma & BioPharma Applications are invited for the following position: Title of Post: Senior Research Fellow in Participatory Health Research – Pharma & BioPharma JOB SYNOPSIS This is a Senior Research Fellow role in UL's RINN Pharma and Biopharma Centre. The job involves building capacity for participatory health research in the Centre and supporting new research collaborations. Faculty of Education & Health Sciences School of Medicine Contract Type: Specific Purpose Salary Scale: €81,760 - €87,743 per annum pro rata (maximum starting salary €81,760) p.a. pro rata University of Limerick is a research-led, energetic and enterprising institution with a proud record of innovation and excellence in education and scholarships. We value creativity, curiosity and excellence in our inclusive community which is committed to social good. Our motto Eagna chun Gnímh translates as Wisdom for Action reflecting our mission to contribute to the discovery of new knowledge for a better world. Informal enquiries regarding the post may be directed to: Professor Anne MacFarlane Primary Healthcare Research School of Medicine University of Limerick Email: anne.macfarlane@ul.ie The closing date for receipt of applications is Tuesday, 27th October 2026 Applications must be completed online before 12 noon, Irish Standard Time on the closing date. Please note your application must include: A letter of introduction and a current CV indicating how you meet the criteria outlined in the Job description. A completed online application form. Please email erecruitment@ul.ie if you experience any difficulties Applications are welcome from suitably qualified candidates. Further information for applicants and application material is available online from: University of Limerick Vacancies We are committed to upholding the principles of fairness, equality, and transparency in pay, in line with the E